# {{TITLE_TEXT}}

This is a lightweight LaTeX-authored mathematics notebook using the synchronized
ElegantBook syntax. `main.tex` and `chapters/*.tex` are the authority; preview
always goes through Typst HTML.

```sh
make edit    # open the configured VS Code workspace
make         # convert main.tex and chapters, then compile index.html
make watch   # continuously preview the generated Typst HTML
```

Ultra Math Preview may render only the formula at the cursor. The synchronized
ElegantBook adapter writes a
self-contained projection under ignored `build/typst/`.
Use `\kn{canonical concept}` for the one authoritative graph occurrence and
`\knref{canonical concept}` elsewhere; both convert to Typst graph markers.
Publishing and graph ingestion are handled later by the repository's
multi-source export skill. Never generate a PDF below `notes/`.
